! Silicon with a PBE norm-conserving pseudopotential: the first gradient-corrected case.
!
! Everything except the functional is the norm-conserving path that already
! reproduces QE to 1e-8 Ry, so a discrepancy here is the gradient correction and
! nothing else. Si.pbe-rrkj is generated with PBE, so no input_dft override is
! involved and the functional comes from the pseudopotential's own header --
! which is the path a normal run takes and which, until GGA existed, silently
! ran this dataset under LDA.
!
! ecutwfc is 20 rather than the 12 the LDA cases use: the rrkj dataset is harder,
! and a gradient correction is evaluated pointwise on the density grid, so an
! under-converged density shows up in it first.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-rrkj.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS
  2
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
   0.250000  0.250000  0.750000   3.00
